  "id": "autoshaping",
  "term": "autoshaping",
  "definition": "Autoshaping is a Pavlovian/instrumental learning procedure in which an organism acquires a new operant response around a conditioned stimulus linked to a reward. It involves forming a conditioned stimulus–unconditioned stimulus association and the transfer of incentive value from the reward to that cue.",
